string.text:
Looks like Spirit can’t find the spirit to escape the alcoholism that recent events in the Zone have helped him fall into. He said he can spare some gear if I bring him Nemiroff vodka. He seems desperate enough to take it in portions, too. If I figure it right, one bottle makes about three portions, hmm...
All right, let’s see:
 • 5 portions of Nemiroff: 4 packs of 9x18 mm;
 • 5 portions of Nemiroff: 2 packs of 5.45x39 mm;
 • 10 portions of Nemiroff: 4 packs of 5.45x39 mm;
 • 10 portions of Nemiroff: 3 packs of 12x70 buckshot;
 • 10 portions of Nemiroff: 1 pack of 7.62x54 mm 7N1;
 • 5 full bottles of Nemiroff plus 7,000 on top: 3 cases of 7.62x54 mm R;
 • 20 portions of Nemiroff: Berill body armor.

Suitcase says he can trade ammunition for other types. Hmm… Apparently he exchanges surplus rounds for the kinds he needs, but who knows with him...
Here’s what he jotted down:
 • He swears he’ll give 200 rounds of 9x19 mm for 200 rounds of 9x18 +P+;
 • He wants 300 rounds of 5.56x45 mm for 300 rounds of 5.45x39 mm;
 • 20 F-1 grenades for 20 M209 grenades;
 • And 10 RGD-5 grenades for 3 RPG rounds.
